From 23a277206ace7c26cc0508fbe5cdea6aa22f6a55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:00:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(apk): support the apk-tools 3 database location and keep
 name aliases

Two changes to the apk analyzer, independent of any particular distro.

apk-tools 3 moved the installed database from /lib/apk/db/installed to
/var/lib/apk/db/installed, and distributions that ship it have no /lib/apk
compatibility symlink, so images built on apk-tools 3 were scanned as
having no OS packages. Add the new location and bump the analyzer version.

The analyzer already parsed the "p:" (provides) field, but only to resolve
the dependency graph. Advisories are published against source package
names, and a package distributed under a name other than the one it is
built from has the provides field as the only link between the two. Keep
those aliases on the package. Namespaced capabilities ("so:libz.so.1",
"cmd:apk", "pc:sqlite3") and paths ("/bin/sh") are not package names and
are left out.
